@startuml deployment
!include _style.iuml
title Deployment and where things live (per Windows user)

node "Microsoft Store" as Store
node "Windows PC" {
  node "MSIX package MarflowSoftware.TextTemplateManager\n(C:\\Program Files\\WindowsApps, read-only)" as Pkg {
    artifact "ttm2.exe\n(.NET 8 self-contained)" as Exe
    artifact "Assets\\editor\\*.html\n(TipTap bundles)" as EditorAssets
    artifact "Assets\\translator\n(Bergamot engine, worker)" as TranslatorAssets
    artifact "Manual.pdf, release.md, LICENSE" as Docs
  }
  node "Framework package\nMicrosoft.WindowsAppRuntime.1.8" as WinAppSdk
  node "Microsoft Edge WebView2 Runtime" as WebView2
  folder "%LocalAppData%\\Packages\\MarflowSoftware.TextTemplateManager_eb1r5ey0kd4ny\\LocalState" as LocalState {
    file "data.ttmdata"
    file "settings.ttmsettings"
    file "sync.ttmsettings"
    file "crash.log"
    file "update.log, update-attempt.json"
    folder "restore-work (only during a restore)"
  }
  folder "%LocalAppData%\\Packages\\MarflowSoftware.TextTemplateManager_eb1r5ey0kd4ny\\LocalCache" as LocalCache {
    folder "TranslationModels\\<from>-<to>"
  }
  folder "Documents\\TextTemplateManager\\Backups" as Backups {
    file "ttm-backup-<kind>-<time>.zip"
  }
  folder "%LocalAppData%\\Marflow Software\\TextTemplateManager\n(TextTemplateManager 1, read only)" as V1
  folder "OneDrive / network share" as Shared {
    file "team.ttmdata (sync file)"
  }
  node "Browser + TTM-Connect extension" as Ext
}

Store --> Pkg : installs; stages updates
Exe --> Store : checks, downloads updates;\nregisters the staged one (Restart to update)
Store --> WinAppSdk : framework dependency
Exe --> WinAppSdk
Exe --> WebView2
Exe --> LocalState : read/write
WebView2 --> LocalCache : reads models
Exe --> Backups : write, read for restore
Exe --> V1 : read once (v1 backup, import)
Exe <--> Shared : sync (merge, write back)
Ext --> Exe : HTTP 127.0.0.1:47615 + token
note right of LocalState
  Removed by Windows on Reset and Uninstall.
  TTM_DATA_DIR redirects all of this
  (and Backups, TTM1) for tests and dev runs.
end note
note right of Backups
  Outside the package: survives Reset,
  Uninstall and reinstall.
end note
@enduml
